# Settings for latency-monitor. `make run` copies this to .env on the first run,
# so edit .env, not this file.
#
# Precedence, weakest first:
#   1. the built-in defaults, which are exactly the values below
#   2. this .env file
#   3. a real environment variable
#   4. a command-line flag
#
# So a one-off run needs no edit at all:
#   KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP=kafka:29092 go run . p1-asks
#   go run . --brokers kafka:29092 p1-asks
#
# The names match warmup/.env.example on purpose — one .env copies between them.

# --- Endpoints -------------------------------------------------------------
# Reached from the HOST, not from inside the containers: docker-compose.yml and
# docker-compose.prod.yml both publish 9092 and 8082.
#
# Running this INSIDE the docker network instead? Use the internal addresses:
#   KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP=kafka:29092
#   SCHEMA_REGISTRY_URL=http://schema-registry:8082
KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP=localhost:9092
SCHEMA_REGISTRY_URL=http://localhost:8082
